17	 
18	 The map is generated from an ASCII sketch of one quarter, `assets/source/maps/sliceSeaSketch.ts`: edit it, then run `npm run map:build -- --from-sketch` (details in `assets/source/maps/README.md`). The `.tmj` stays within the Tiled subset documented in `packages/content/src/tiledMap.ts`, so [Tiled](https://www.mapeditor.org/) opens it.
19	 
20	-`PIRATE_SEA_RACE_TEST_PLACEMENT=1` is a test-only setting, off by default: the dev and test entry point (`npm run dev`, and the server the browser tests start) then serves `POST /__test/place`, which puts a player's ship on a chosen tile. `PIRATE_SEA_RACE_TEST_SOURCES` (for example `sun,sun|moon,moon|sun,sun|moon,moon`, each island's source types) is another, off by default: every match then deals its rubbings in that layout instead of the private shuffle. The production entry (`npm start`) reads neither.
21	+`PIRATE_SEA_RACE_TEST_PLACEMENT=1` is a test-only setting, off by default: the dev and test entry point (`npm run dev`, and the server the browser tests start) then serves `POST /__test/place`, which puts a player's ship on a chosen tile. The others, also off by default: `PIRATE_SEA_RACE_TEST_SOURCES` (for example `sun,sun|moon,moon|sun,sun|moon,moon`, each island's source types) deals every match's rubbings in that layout instead of the private shuffle; `PIRATE_SEA_RACE_TEST_TIMINGS` (for example `ready=60,protection=20,match=12000`, in world ticks, 20 a second; also `sectors` and `carriers` for the two timed reveals) shortens the countdown, the departure protection, the match and its reveals; `PIRATE_SEA_RACE_TEST_FINAL_SECRET` (a 32-bit number) pins the secret that picks the final island. With the placement setting on, `POST /__test/next-match-timings` (for example `{"match": 400}`) also gives the next match created its own timings. The production entry (`npm start`) reads none of them.
22	 
23	 The integration tests run in two groups (`npm run test:integration`): most files in parallel worker processes, with test-only shorter timings, then the netcode harness files (`duelHarness`, `seaDuelHarness`, `devLatency`) one after another on a quiet machine.
